    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the inboard flap track number two support structure at the wing rear spar, drawn as one attachment standard with the three-bolt rib and its six barrel nuts per side.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the flap support rib, the rear spar interface fitting and the attachment hardware for the inboard flap track number two position, on the left and right wing.",
      "figure_note": "The view is a section through the rear spar looking outboard, with the flap removed. One rib standard is shown, recognised by its plain web and its three attachment holes, and no alternate item appears on the figure. The barrel nuts at item 70 are used six per side. The protective sleeves at item 110 are fitted at every bolt position. Left and right are identical."
    },
