    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the inboard flap track number two support structure at the wing rear spar, showing the three-bolt and the reinforced five-bolt attachment standards as alternate items.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the flap support rib, the rear spar interface fitting and the attachment hardware for the inboard flap track number two position, on the left and right wing.",
      "figure_note": "The view is a section through the rear spar looking outboard, with the flap removed. Items 20 and 20A are the two rib standards and are recognised by the web thickness and by the number of attachment holes; the reinforced rib also carries the upper cleat at item 50, which does not exist on the original standard. Neither rib supersedes the other on the figure. Each is listed as an alternate keyed to the standard fitted, because both fly and a station has to be able to order for either. The barrel nuts at item 70 are common to both standards but the reinforced attachment uses ten instead of six per side. The protective sleeves at item 110 are deleted on the reinforced standard, where the bolt shanks are sleeved at manufacture. Left and right are identical apart from the handed cleat."
    },
